    "senderName": "NWS Honolulu HI",
    "headline": "Flood Advisory issued October 8 at 9:53PM HST until October 9 at 12:45AM HST by NWS Honolulu HI",
    "description": "* WHAT...Flooding caused by excessive rainfall is expected.\n\n* WHERE...Southeast slopes of the Big Island of Hawaii...\n\n* WHEN...Until 1245 AM HST.\n\n* IMPACTS...Minor flooding on roads, poor drainage areas, and in\nstreams.\n\n* ADDITIONAL DETAILS...\n- At 947 PM HST, Doppler radar indicated heavy rain over Kau and\nPuna Districts. Minor flooding is ongoing or expected to begin\nshortly in the advisory area. Rain was falling at a rate of 0.5\nto 1 inch per hour.\n- Some locations that will experience flooding include...\nHawaii Volcanoes National Park, Wood Valley, Pahala, Volcano,\nPunaluu Beach, Kawa Flats, Glenwood, Naalehu, Mountain View and\nFern Forest.",
    "instruction": "Stay away from streams, drainage ditches and low lying areas prone to\nflooding.\n\nDo not cross fast flowing or rising water in your vehicle, or on\nfoot. Turn around, don't drown.",
